# # User Manager - Complete Usage Guide

# ## Overview

# The `UserManager` provides a comprehensive API for managing users with powerful filtering, creation, and bulk operations.

# ## Basic Usage

# ```python
# from django.contrib.auth import get_user_model

# User = get_user_model()
# ```

# ---

# ## User Creation

# ### Create Regular User

# ```python
# # Create user with email
# user = User.objects.create_user(
#     email_or_phone='user@example.com',
#     password='securepass123'
# )

# # Create user with phone
# user = User.objects.create_user(
#     email_or_phone='+12025551234',
#     password='securepass123'
# )

# # Create user with additional fields
# user = User.objects.create_user(
#     email_or_phone='user@example.com',
#     password='securepass123',
#     user_timezone='America/New_York'
# )
# ```

# ### Create Superuser

# ```python
# # Create admin user
# admin = User.objects.create_superuser(
#     email_or_phone='admin@example.com',
#     password='adminpass123'
# )

# # Automatically sets:
# # - is_staff=True
# # - is_superuser=True
# # - role='admin'
# ```

