# ## Best Practices

# 1. **Always use manager methods** instead of raw queries
# 2. **Chain filters** for complex queries
# 3. **Use bulk operations** for performance
# 4. **Run cleanup tasks** regularly via cron/celery
# 5. **Monitor statistics** for insights
# 6. **Soft delete first**, permanently delete later
# 7. **Test thoroughly** before bulk operations

# ---

# ## Performance Tips

# ```python
# # ✅ Good: Use select_related for foreign keys
# users = User.objects.active().select_related('profile')

# # ✅ Good: Use prefetch_related for many-to-many
# users = User.objects.active().prefetch_related('groups')

# # ✅ Good: Use only() for specific fields
# users = User.objects.active().only('email_or_phone', 'role')

# # ✅ Good: Use values() for dictionaries
# user_data = User.objects.active().values('email_or_phone', 'created_at')

# # ❌ Avoid: N+1 queries
# for user in User.objects.all():
#     print(user.groups.all())  # Queries in loop!

# # ✅ Better: Prefetch
# for user in User.objects.prefetch_related('groups'):
#     print(user.groups.all())  # No extra queries
# ```